{"study_accession":"PRJNA693819","secondary_study_accession":"SRP302704","title":"Distinct transcriptional profile of blood mononuclear cells in Behcet’s disease: insights into the central role of neutrophil chemotaxis","description":"Both innate and adaptive immune responses are reportedly increased in Behcet’s disease (BD), a chronic-relapsing systemic vasculitis lying at the intersection between autoinflammation and autoimmunity. To further study pathophysiologic molecular mechanisms operating in BD we searched for transcriptome-wide changes in blood mononuclear cells from these patients. We performed 3’ mRNA next generation sequencing-based genome-wide transcriptional profiling followed by analysis of differential expression signatures, KEGG pathways, GO biological processes and transcription factor signatures al 25 samples (11 healthy controls and 14 BD). Overall design: 25 human samples out of with 11 healthy controls and 14 with Behcet’s disease","pubmed":"33493315","geo_series":"","n_samples":25,"study_labels":[{"level":"study","event_code":"AUTOIMMUNE_FLARE","certainty":"confirmed","delta_days":-60.0,"delta_bucket":"B_FAR","time_precision":"approx","stage":"teacher","confidence":1.0,"evidence":"Both innate and adaptive immune responses are reportedly increased in Behcet’s disease (BD), a chronic-relapsing systemic vasculitis lying at the intersection between autoinflammation and autoimmunity.","model_version":"teacher:mlx:mlx-community/Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct-4bit"}],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN17477972","study_accession":"PRJNA693819","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"HC6","description":"HC6","sex":"female","geo_sample":"GSM5028907","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-05-27","attributes":[["source_name","PBMCs"],["tissue","Blood"],["age","31"],["sex","female"],["disease","Healthy"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR13496937","experiment_accession":"SRX9908858","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","i